    // We scale this penalty by progress to be more conservative as we approach the end of the stream.
    // Near the end, we want to consolidate bins rather than open new ones.
    if is_new_bin {
        // The base cost of opening a new bin is the capacity.
        // We add a non-linear penalty that grows as the stream progresses to discourage bin creation.
        score += bin_capacity as f64 * (1.0 + progress.powi(2) * 2.0);

        // If there are other bins that could fit this, penalize opening a new one heavily.
        if fitting_bins_count > 0 {
